The problem isn't just one insurrection, it's

00:00:12.531 --> 00:00:15.210
mass radicalization.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:21.820
And in this article, Zach writes that, quote,
Experts say the attack, meaning January 6th

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:27.240
riot, is hugely worrying for reasons beyond
what the Senate is debating, unlike other

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.269
recent spasms of American violence.

00:00:30.269 --> 00:00:33.960
This was not the work of a lone wolf nor of
a small cell of radicals.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:39.550
The pathway to an attempted government overthrow
unfolded in public out loud on the Internet

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:43.410
in a process that experts call mass radicalization.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:46.820
We've been talking about how do you mass deprogram
people?

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:51.170
Zach Stanton is accurately talking about how
there has been a mass radicalization that

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:52.450
has taken place.

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:58.420
I would argue that Trump winning the Republican
primary was already an example of that back

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:04.729
in 2016 about the degree to which the Republican
Party had been deemed intellectualized and

00:01:04.729 --> 00:01:06.310
mass radicalized.

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:10.400
Arzak goes on to say, the protest was largely
just the tip of the iceberg.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:15.920
No one knows how many Americans, tens of thousands
more would willingly have joined them if they'd

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.050
been in Washington that day.

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:22.070
It's a new challenge for America and a serious
one at times and places when large groups

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:27.260
of people have been inspired to embrace violence,
it often leads to long term unrest, if not

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:28.810
outright civil war.

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:32.180
And right now, experts think it's happening
faster than ever.

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:35.030
We talked about this almost verbatim.

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:42.350
Michael Jensen, an expert on extremism, said
historically mass radicalization took time,

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:44.670
